        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ad3a2794-9615-5a76-9e10-e24bc08e0913",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sydney Anderson\n- Places: Zumbrota, Goodhue County, Minneapolis, Hennepin County, Des Moines, Kansas City, Lanesboro, Minnesota, Iowa, Missouri\n- Roles: U.S. Representative, lawyer, private\n- Organizations: Highland Park College, University of Minnesota, Minnesota Volunteer Infantry\n- Events: Spanish–American War\n- Topics: Minneapolis\n\nFacts:\n- Sydney Anderson was born on September 18, 1881, in Zumbrota, Goodhue County, Minnesota.\n- Sydney Anderson attended common schools, graduated from high school in 1899, attended Highland Park College in Des Moines, Iowa, and attended the University of Minnesota in Minneapolis.\n- During the Spanish–American War, Sydney Anderson served as a private in Company D of the Fourteenth Regiment, Minnesota Volunteer Infantry.\n- Sydney Anderson studied law, was admitted to the bar in 1903, and began practicing law in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n- From 1904 to 1911, Sydney Anderson practiced law after moving from Minneapolis to Kansas City, Missouri, and then to Lanesboro, Minnesota.\n- Sydney Anderson later served as a Representative from Minnesota.\n- Minneapolis is the county seat of Hennepin County.\n- Minneapolis is the larger of the Twin Cities and is part of the 16th-largest metropolitan area in the United States.\n- Sydney Anderson died on October 8, 1948.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9aaa34f1-af65-519e-a018-910dcc6bf1a2",
        "text": "Page: Sydney Anderson. Sentence: Sydney Anderson (September 18, 1881 – October 8, 1948) was a Representative from Minnesota; born in Zumbrota, Minnesota, Goodhue County, Minnesota; attended the common schools; was graduated from high school in 1899; attended Highland Park College, Des Moines, Iowa, and the University of Minnesota at Minneapolis; studied law; was admitted to the bar in 1903 and commenced practice in Minneapolis, Minnesota; moved to Kansas City, Missouri, and thence to Lanesboro, Minnesota, and continued the practice of law from 1904–1911; served as a private in Company D, Fourteenth Regiment, Minnesota Volunteer Infantry, during the Spanish–American War.\nPage: Minneapolis. Sentence: Minneapolis ( ) is the county seat of Hennepin County, and the larger of the Twin Cities, the 16th-largest metropolitan area in the United States.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
